Wave 3 invariants — locked by `src/test/safety/safetyPerfCapaWave3.test.ts`.

## Training cache invalidation (POLICY §110)

Training mutations in `useSafetyTraining.ts` MUST NOT invalidate the bare
`['safety','training']` sub-root. The legitimate scopes are:

- `useUpsertSop` → `['safety','training','sops']` + `['safety','training','sop', id]`.
- `useDeleteSop` → above + `quiz-for-sop,id` + `assignments,by-sop,id`.
- `useUpsertQuiz` → `quiz-for-sop, sopId` + `questions, quizId`.
- `useUpsertQuestion` → `questions, quizId`.
- `useDeleteQuestion` → `['safety','training','questions']` (quiz_id unknown).
- `useAssignSopToRole`, `useStartTrainingAttempt`, `useSubmitTrainingAttempt`
  → `['safety','training','assignments']`.

## Caps

`useSopAssignments` is capped at 500 rows via `.range(0, 499)`. Do not raise
the cap — if a single SOP exceeds 500 assignments, paginate the UI instead.

## Permits primitives

`src/pages/safety/SafetyPermits.tsx` MUST use `useManualQuery`,
`SafetyFilterSheet`, `SafetyResponsiveList`, `SafetyMobileListCard`,
`SafetyStickyActionBar`, `SafetySkeletonBlock`, and scoped realtime on
`['safety_permits', 'safety_permit_approvals']` only.
